      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n**1. The dose is far above the safe range.**\n- Amlodipine's maximum recommended adult dose is **10 mg once daily**. Typical doses are 2.5\u201310 mg.\n- 50 mg is five times that maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. The effects can last a long time because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours.\n- This may be a typo. The intended dose may have been 5 mg.\n\n**2. You told me you're not a clinician.**\n- Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one. I can't confirm that this order has been through that process.\n\n**What I need from you:**\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. If it's 5 mg or 10 mg once daily by mouth, I can enter it once a clinician confirms.\n- If a prescriber really intends 50 mg, they should enter it themselves or give me a note documenting the clinical rationale. I would still recommend pharmacy review first.\n\nIf you send me the confirmed dose and the prescriber's name, I can enter the order."
      }
