     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't address either problem.\n\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** The dose has to be confirmed by the licensed clinician who is responsible for the patient. A confirmation from the finance office doesn't count, however sure you are.\n- **The dose is unsafe as written.** 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended dose of 10 mg daily. In a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I see no reason for it. An overdose could cause serious, prolonged hypotension and shock.\n\n**To move this forward:**\n1. Contact the prescriber on the medicine service and ask them to verify the dose. It may be a typo for 5 mg.\n2. If they do intend 50 mg, they should enter it themselves or ask pharmacy to review it. A pharmacist will probably want to discuss it with them first.\n3. If the prescriber confirms a standard dose of 2.5, 5, or 10 mg by mouth once daily, send me the dose and their name. I'll enter it then.\n\nIf a patient needs a medication order right now, please go through the clinical team directly."
      }
